{
 "id": "0e5c1ea3-a38f-4c61-86e2-0459dc8f61a4",
 "type": "manga",
 "attributes": {
  "title": {
   "en": "Horror Manga Short Stories: Loneliness"
  },
  "altTitles": [
   {
    "ja-ro": "Kyoufu Manga Tanpenshuu: Kodoku"
   },
   {
    "ja": "恐怖漫画短編集 孤独"
   }
  ],
  "description": {
   "en": "Do you have any manga that has traumatic memories? Here you will find genuine horror manga that is being lost due to regulations and self-restraint. This book is a compilation of masterpieces by 10 top horror manga artists that have not yet been published in book form. You will be struck by a fear that can only be read here. Horror manga fans will rejoice, and those who are experiencing horror manga for the first time will open the door to a new world. Be sure to line your bookshelf with this book. This is the scariest, craziest, and strongest horror manga anthology.\n\nCover: Amagappa Shoujogun\nFrontispiece: Taniguchi Tomoo\nTable of Contents: Takatsuka Q\n\n1. Inagaki Misao: Beyond the Window (Horror M, February 1997 issue)\n2. Sugihara Natsuki: Mama's Hamburgers (Horror M, August 2002 issue)\n3. Mayama Sou: The Island I Yearn for (Horror M, October 2007 issue)\n4. Takayama Tatari: Mirror Man (Manuscript published September 2013)\n5. Katou Yagi + Yagi Jun: Mountain Child  (Big Comic Spirits Special: Spirits Casual, August, 2005 issue)\n6. Kanda Moriri: A Non-Human Baby (AC Labien Special: Kyoufu Mystery, May 1991 issue)\n7. Shibahara Mukade: Stab!  (Horror M, May 2007 issue)\n8. Watanabe Yasuhiro: The Damp Room (Mystery DX Special: The Horror, August 1997 issue)\n9. Ozu Tetsuya: DREAM  (Kyoufu no Kairaku, April 1997 issue)\n10. Kondou Soushin: Stranger Danger (Kyoufu no Kairaku, February 2004 issue)"
  },
